<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH UNADJUSTED UNEMPLOYMENT RISES IN MAY-JULY.</title>
<headline>DUTCH UNADJUSTED UNEMPLOYMENT RISES IN MAY-JULY.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch</p>
<p>non-seasonally adjusted unemployment rose to an average of</p>
<p>378,000 in May-July from 376,000 in April-June 1997, the Central</p>
<p>Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT NON-SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   May-July 97   April-June 96   May-July 96</p>
<p> total number	   378,000	  376,000	  415,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    5.7		5.6		6.2</p>
<p>DUTCH REGISTERED UNEMPLOYMENT SEASONALLY ADJUSTED</p>
<p>			   May-July 97   April-June 97   May-July 96</p>
<p> total number	   395,000	  395,000	  432,000</p>
<p> pct of labour force    5.9		5.9		6.5</p>
<p>NOTES - Percentages are calculated in relation to average</p>
<p>1996 labour force (6.681 mln). By international standards, the</p>
<p>CBS uses a narrow definition of unemployment. Figures are</p>
<p>compiled from job centre registrations and CBS survey.</p>
<p>Economists polled by Reuters before publication of the</p>
<p>figures had expected a non-seasonally adjusted May-July</p>
<p>unemployment figure of around 375,000 and a seasonally adjusted</p>
<p>figure of around 389,000.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
